	\caption{(a) Boundary tiles (dark cyan) and non-boundary tiles (gray). (b) Every step of the  algorithm adds a tile in two steps: (1)~Move a new tile $t$ to a boundary position $p$ of $P$ that is free. (2)~Move $t$ on $P$ from $p$ to a position that is adjacent to a tile of the current polyomino $P'$. (c) The curve $B$ (blue), and the set $T$ (orange).}
	\label{fig:approx}
