A stronger provenance audit changes the outcome: the affine tags and shear program make the solver recover a benchmark-invented algebraic key, not a construction object supplied by the paper. The geometry becomes an easy monotone path covered by Theorem 13/Corollary 14, so the apparent Track B gap is manufactured by auxiliary encoding. I’m rejecting the family on H, retaining the experimental generator under the required `rejected_gen_…` name, and documenting both its local measurements and why they do not establish a valid paper family.
