207,328
Rejected at Step 0: no paper-faithful family satisfies H under either track.

- Track A: Theorem 7 proves worst-case NP-completeness for specialized 3D reduction gadgets, not inverse-generated random assembly sequences.
- Track B: the native tree algorithm performs only comparable work to the required explicit witness—about 384 state visits versus at least 255 unit moves at the output cap. There is no meaningful compression gap.
- The experimental affine-tag construction passed local G1–G8, but its difficulty came from an artificial finite-field decoder absent from the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.05784), so it was not valid native coverage.
- The oracle run had zero scored attempts because OpenRouter returned four HTTP 403 quota errors.

